rbonate</td><td>2.2</td><td>0.85</td><td>—</td><td>2.2</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sodium Chloride</td><td>6.8</td><td>6.8</td><td>8.0</td><td>6.8</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sodium Phosphate Dibasic (anhydrous)</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>0.04788</td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sodium Phosphate Monobasic (anhydrous)</td><td>0.122</td><td>0.122</td><td>—</td><td>0.122</td></tr>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - First Culturing Guidance_20250401°í´.docx (https://cellbank.nibn.go.jp/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/jcrb/What-media-should-I-use_20250401.pdf)\nciteturn37search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; <th>Sigma Aldrich (Merck, Millipore)</th> ... <td>Eagle's minimum essential medium, EMEM, E-MEM</td> ... <td>M4655</td>\nJCRB Cell Bank essentially uses the media with standard formulation.  \nThe following table shows the example of liquid media products with standard formulation.\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th>Fujifilm Wako</th>\n<th>GIBCO (Thermofisher)</th>\n<th>Sigma Aldrich (Merck, Millipore)</th>\n<th>Corning</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>MEM</b></td>\n<td>Eagle's minimum essential medium, EMEM, E-MEM</td>\n<td>051-07615</td>\n<td>11095-080</td>\n<td>M4655</td>\n<td>10-010-CV</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>MEM with NEAA</b></td>\n<td>Eagle's minimum essential medium with non-essential amino acids</td>\n<td>055-08975</td>\n<td>10370-021 (add L-glutamine to 2 mM)</td>\n<td>M0325, M5650 (add L-glutamine to 2 mM)</td>\n<td>10-009-CV</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>MEM alpha</b></td>\n<td>alpha MEM, αMEM alpha modification of MEM</td>\n<td>137-17215</td>\n<td>12571-063</td>\n<td>M8042 (add L-glutamine to 2 mM)</td>\n<td>10-022-CV</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>DMEM (low glucose) [standard DMEM]</b></td>\n<td>Dulbecco's modified Eagle's medium, D-MEM, DME</td>\n<td>041-29775</td>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMinimum Essential Medium Eagle (MEM) with Earle s salts, L-glutamine and sodium bicarbonate sterile filtered Sigma-Aldrich (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/m4655?%C2%A0%3B+region=US)\nciteturn37search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; M4655 ... Image: Sigma-Aldrich ... Minimum Essential Medium (MEM), developed by Harry Eagle, is one of the most widely used of all synthetic cell culture media.\n\nM4655\n\nImage: Minimum Essential Medium Eagle With Earle&#8242;s salts, L-glutamine and sodium bicarbonate, liquid, sterile-filtered, suitable for cell culture\n\n1 Video\n\nM4655\n\nImage: Sigma-Aldrich\n\nShare\n\n# Minimum Essential Medium Eagle\n\n## With Earle′s salts, L-glutamine and sodium bicarbonate, liquid, sterile-filtered, suitable for cell culture\n\n5.0\n\n### Select a Size\n\nChange View\n\nSize/SKU  | Availability  | Price\n--- | --- | ---\n500 mL M4655-500ML  | Check Cart for Availability  | $38.90\n1 L M4655-1L  | Available to ship TODAY from MILWAUKEE  | $62.80\n6 x 500 mL M4655-6X500ML  | Check Cart for Availability  | $203.00\n24 x 500 mL M4655-24X500ML  | Check Cart for Availability  | $731.00\n\n### About This Item\n\nNACRES:\n\nNA.75\n\nUNSPSC Code:\n\n12352207\n\n## M4655-500ML\n\n### $38.90\n\n* * *\n\nCheck Cart for Availability\n\n* * *\n\nProperties\n\n### Quality Segment\n\n400\n\n### sterility\n\nsterile-filtered\n\n### form\n\nliquid\n\n### technique(s)\n\ncell culture | mammalian: suitable\n\n### impurities\n\nendotoxin, tested\n\n### components\n\nsodium pyruvate: no\nphenol red: yes\nEarle’s salts (5% CO_{2}): yes\nHEPES: no\nNaHCO_{3}: yes\nL-glutamine: yes\n\n### shipped in\n\nambient\n\n### storage temp.\n\n2-8°C\n\nDescription\n\n### General description\n\nListen to an Audio Overview\nMinimum Essential Medium (MEM), developed by Harry Eagle, is one of the most widely used of all synthetic cell culture media. Early attempts to cultivate normal mammalian fibroblasts and certain subtypes of HeLa cells revealed they had specific nutritional requirements that could not be met by Eagle’s Basal Medium (BME). Subsequent studies using these and other cells in culture indicated additions to BME could be made to aid growth of a wider variety of fastidious cells.\nMEM, which incorporates these modifications, includes higher concentrations of amino acids so the medium more closely approximates the protein composition of cultured mammalian cells. MEM has been used for cultivation of a wide variety of cells grown in monolayers. Optional supplementation of non-essential amino acids to the formulations that incorporate either Hanks’ or Earle’s salts has broadened the usefulness of this medium.\n\n### Application\n\nGenerally used to grow attached cell lines, such as fibroblasts, in the presence of FBS, calf or horse sera.\n\n### Other Notes\n\nThis product lacks L-Ala; L-Asn; L-Glu; Gly; L-Pro; L-Ser.\n\n* * *\n\n## Safety Information\n\n### Storage Class\n\n12 - Non Combustible Liquids\n\n### wgk\n\nWGK 1\n\n### flash_point_f\n\nNot applicable\n\n### flash_point_c\n\nNot applicable\n\n## Documentation\n\n[Button: Certificate of Analysis][Button: Certificate of Origin]\n\n* * *\n\nChoose from one of the most recent versions:\n\n### Certificates of Analysis (COA)\n\nLot/Batch Number\n\nIt looks like we've run into a problem, but you can still download Certificates of Analysis from our Documents section.\n\nIf you need assistance, please contact Customer Support\n\n### Already Own This Product?\n\nFind documentation for the products that you have recently purchased in the Document Library.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGibco Peptones for Bioprocessing - US (https://www.thermofisher.com/us/en/home/bioprocessing/products/cell-culture/feeds-supplements/peptones.html)\nciteturn37search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; 211910  | Polypeptone™ Peptone, 454 g  | Each  | 229.00  | [Button: -] [Input] [Button: +] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [I